  "name": "Melting Bernini: Noise as Sculptor",
  "title": "Noise Extruded to Terrain",
  "lookup_name": "Noise_Columns",
  "description": "Three columns in one frame, the same mesh at the same resolution, the same material and the same mapped displacement range, differing only in what drives the melt: one held at a fixed phase, one on the shipped sine, and one on a real coherent field seeded by the room. Which is which is not written anywhere until a visitor presses REVEAL. The instrument logs both drivers and their displacement at the same moment; FREEZE stops time so the geometry can be inspected and repeated, SPIN turns a column without deforming it, MARBLE takes the veined shader off so material noise cannot be mistaken for the geometric driver. The columns carry no collider and hold nothing up. Corrected 2026-09-12: the previous description named an erosion process and an undoing of disorder that the shipped melt never implemented, the melt having been a sine with no field in it at all.",
